# Downloaded stand binaries (see docs/CAPTURE.md — taken from the fingerproxy releases)
tools/*.exe
tools/echo-server_*
tools/fingerproxy_*

# The private key of the self-signed certificate — generated locally
capture/certs/tls.key
capture/certs/tls.crt

# Raw capture samples: bulky and reproducible; only the normalised reference
# from reference/ goes into the repository
capture/samples/

# The curl-impersonate source corpus: downloaded by ./cmd/import, only the
# profiles derived from it go into the repository, in profiles/
corpus/

# References taken from the local stand: they depend on the machine and the
# certificate. References from the public oracle (reference/baselines/) are
# the opposite — those are committed.
reference/baselines-local/

# Go / the native build.
#
# vendor/ is NOT ignored: it is committed on purpose. utls and uquic are pinned
# to pseudo-versions on master, because upstream does not tag the fresh parrots.
# A pseudo-version is a pin — it names a commit and go.sum locks its hash — but
# it survives only as long as that commit does. Vendoring makes the build
# independent of the upstream repositories continuing to exist.
dist/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.h

# okhttp probe: the jars are fetched from Maven Central, the classes are built
capture/okhttp/lib/
capture/okhttp/*.class

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
.pytest_cache/

# Filled in during the wheel build: the native library and a copy of the profiles.
# The sources live in dist/ and profiles/ respectively.
python/curlpro/lib/
python/curlpro/profiles/
python/LICENSE
python/NOTICE
python/dist/
